<p>A UN-mandated independent fact-finding mission says abuses committed during the Rapid Support Forces (RSF) siege and capture of El Fasher, capital of Sudan’s North Darfur state, carried the “hallmarks of genocide.” The mission found signs that the RSF and allied militias acted with genocidal intent toward non-Arab communities such as the Zaghawa and Fur. The report describes ethnically targeted killings, rape and other sexual violence, enforced disappearances, and the deliberate creation of conditions meant to destroy parts of those communities. The mission called for accountability and warned that civilians still face acute danger as fighting shifts, with particular concern for neighboring Kordofan state after El Fasher fell. Sudan’s war—between the army and the RSF, ongoing since April 2023—has killed tens of thousands and forced millions from their homes, fueling what the UN calls one of the world’s worst humanitarian crises. Even amid the grim findings, the report is a concrete step toward documentation and potential justice. Investigators said they collected testimony and other evidence designed to support future prosecutions and protection efforts.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/OkAAnYrKYXsq8eVq161C3_LzMg1NRELVZxdGPreYF51EUIWGopBqbmwuTKxXgmgkj0wUoUu--vxnBB5cAFkwkSU5TJMROnafTw17oKnjDYiBALDtOdSdGCuUp6aPAKgwaRLY6YOcZPo-9vyzDsWkwCmRmttiA55BJWY1cs3ymvmvalxO4Zo2x5fEvyQxNP2PCTxLIO3cILuG-2NvPaqSKzPC4kQsKZHKi2zZkNr6PsmVqtWMWvXLQGqMT2n7OeM5HgzpyhYz7lvFF4iMaA' alt='Sudanese refugee women wait to collect water in Adre, Chad, as the Sudan war drives displacement.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Witness testimony: Investigators said they interviewed 320 witnesses and victims while examining events around El Fasher.</li><li>Harrowing timeframe: The mission said the RSF takeover in October brought “three days of absolute horror,” following a siege that lasted about 18 months.</li><li>Graphic evidence: The UN mission said graphic footage circulating in October appeared to show RSF members carrying out mass killings and other crimes.</li><li>Recent strikes: UNICEF said at least 15 children were killed in a drone strike on a displacement camp in West Kordofan this week; local rights defenders said another strike on a market killed 28 people in North Kordofan.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UN fact-finding mission on Sudan: The mission said the scale, coordination, and senior-level endorsement showed the crimes around El Fasher were not random. It described a planned operation with defining characteristics of genocide and called for urgent civilian protection in Kordofan. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1974539/un-probe-finds-hallmarks-of-genocide-in-sudan'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Human rights experts (UN inquiry): The experts concluded the RSF acted with “genocidal intent” during the months-long siege of El Fasher. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/19/world/africa/sudan-un-el-fasher-rsf.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>UN investigators (Darfur focus): Investigators said the RSF systematically killed and raped members of ethnic groups in El Fasher, warning the findings point to a “renewed” risk of genocide in Darfur. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-un-genocide-rsf-darfur-sudan/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cpqw74d81jqo'>Sudan atrocities are &#x27;hallmarks of genocide&#x27;, UN says</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/hallmark-of-genocide-found-in-sudan-s-el-fasher-un/a-76047495'>&#x27;Hallmark of genocide&#x27; found in Sudan&#x27;s el-Fasher — UN</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/19/world/africa/sudan-un-el-fasher-rsf.html'>Assault on Sudanese City Bore ‘Hallmarks of Genocide,’ U.N. Finds</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-un-genocide-rsf-darfur-sudan/'>UN finds evidence of ‘renewed’ genocide by RSF in Darfur</a> - theg